In the above theorem, adjacent triangles are forbidden in the graph. In the second result of this paper, adjacent triangles are allowed but two triangles sharing exactly one vertex are forbidden. 
\begin{restatable}{theorem}{MRB}\label{MRB}
Let $G$ be a plane graph without subgraphs isomorphic to the configurations in \autoref{F-MR2}, and let $\mathscr{M}$ be a $4$-matching assignment for $G$. If $S$ is the vertices of a $6^{-}$-cycle of $G$, then every $\mathscr{M}$-coloring $\phi$ of $G[S]$ can be extended to an $\mathscr{M}$-coloring $\varphi$ of $G$. 
\end{restatable}

